book instead of creating a duplicate; per-tab header write only happens if the current header row differs from schema; per-tab seeding only happens if the tab has zero data rows, except Configuration which is upserted by key so user edits to existing keys are never overwritten; removes the default empty 'Sheet1' if still empty after setup); selfCheck.gs (runSelfCheck() reads back every tab's header row and diffs against PANEL_OPS_SCHEMA, plus checks Workflow_States row count, Configuration key presence, Loss_Reasons and Users row counts, logging PASS/FAIL per check via Logger.log, matching the ticket's specified verification approach exactly). BLOCKER: this executor's sandbox has no Google Workspace/clasp/OAuth credentials and no way to actually create/open a Google Sheets file or execute Apps Script code (verified: 'which clasp' -> not found; no ~/.clasprc.json reachable -- filesystem access is restricted to this project directory only; no network/OAuth flow available). The ticket's verification commands and 'run evidence' deliverable both require live execution against a real Drive/Sheets file, which is not possible here. I could not even run node --check on the .gs files -- that specific command was denied by the sandbox's Bash permission policy (multiple attempts, including bare node --check <file> and node -e ..., all returned 'This command requires approval' with no interactive approver in this session). As a partial substitute I manually re-verified: (1) every one of the 16 header arrays in schema.gs against data-model.md's table definitions, column-by-column, in order; (2) all 17 Workflow_States seed rows and the full transition matrix against workflow-state-machine.md; (3) brace/paren counts balanced per file (schema.gs 16/16, seeds.gs 31/31, setup.gs 29/29, selfCheck.gs 28/28) as a lightweight syntax sanity check. None of this substitutes for actually running setupPanelOpsWorkbook() + runSelfCheck() inside Apps Script and capturing the PASS/FAIL log, which