h clasp' -> not found; no ~/.clasprc.json reachable -- filesystem access is restricted to this project directory only; no network/OAuth flow available). The ticket's verification commands and 'run evidence' deliverable both require live execution against a real Drive/Sheets file, which is not possible here. I could not even run `node --check` on the .gs files -- that specific command was denied by the sandbox's Bash permission policy (multiple attempts, including bare `node --check <file>` and `node -e ...`, all returned 'This command requires approval' with no interactive approver in this session). As a partial substitute I manually re-verified: (1) every one of the 16 header arrays in schema.gs against data-model.md's table definitions, column-by-column, in order; (2) all 17 Workflow_States seed rows and the full transition matrix against workflow-state-machine.md; (3) brace/paren counts balanced per file (schema.gs 16/16, seeds.gs 31/31, setup.gs 29/29, selfCheck.gs 28/28) as a lightweight syntax sanity check. None of this substitutes for actually running setupPanelOpsWorkbook() + runSelfCheck() inside Apps Script and capturing the PASS/FAIL log, which is what the ticket requires as evidence. To unblock: a human (or an agent with Google account access / clasp login configured) needs to (a) create or open the target Apps Script project bound to a Google account, (b) push these 4 files (clasp push or paste into the Apps Script editor), (c) run setupPanelOpsWorkbook() once from the editor, (d) run runSelfCheck() and share the Logger.log output (or Stackdriver/Execution log) back into this ticket so it can be marked complete against the real acceptance criteria (self-check PASS on all 16 tabs, seeds present, re-run makes no changes).\"}\nJSONL_EOF"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01UEFgXjjdsTQgfgeqh9ZXQM","tool_input":{"command":"python3 -c \"import json,sys; [json.loads(l) for l in open('comments/INF-001.jsonl')]; print('json OK')\""}}],"terminal_reason":