logs/INF-001-2026-07-18T03-42-45-647Z.log:18:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M8m7pvzZVMs25ezzQeYxHa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Roadmap — Panel-Ops\n2\t**Owner:** Architect AI. This file is the authoritative execution plan.\n3\t**Read-only for executors and the dashboard.** Runtime status lives in `roadmap-status.md`.\n4\tBaseline statuses here are descriptive only.\n5\t\n6\tExecutor rules (binding for every ticket): read `comments/<TICKET>.jsonl` first, human\n7\tcomments are binding; implement only the assigned ticket; respect invariants; run\n8\tverification; update `roadmap-status.md`; append completion/blockage comment; never edit\n9\t`roadmap.md`; never touch files outside \"Files allowed to change\".\n10\t\n11\tGlobal invariants (apply to every APP/INF/INT ticket): server-side role enforcement;\n12\tsoft deletes only; append-only Activity; all writes via LockService path; no credentials\n13\tin code; Spanish UI text, English identifiers; schemas exactly per `data-model.md`.\n14\t\n15\tPhases: 0 Discovery · 1 Governance + Operational Control · 2 Parts + Quotation ·\n16\t3 Approval + Payment · 4 Optimizer Exports · 5 AI (not yet ticketed).\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## Phase 0 — Discovery (human tasks, tracked as tickets)\n21\t\n22\t## DIS-001 — Optimizer Format Samples\n23\t\n24\t- Status baseline: pending\n25\t- Recommended model: human (Management/Advisor) — not an agent task\n26\t- Dependencies: none\n27\t- Objective: Obtain real import files accepted by LEPTON and KDT Optimizer plus full format specs.\n28\t- Context: `integration-contracts.md §1–2`. INT-001/INT-002 are hard-blocked on this.\n29\t- Scope: real LEPTON file; real KDT file; exact columns and order; units; decimal separator; delimiter; encoding; grain/rotation rules; material/thickness encoding; edge-band encoding; required vs optional columns.\n30\t- Out of scope: building adapters.\n31\t- Architectural invariants: executors must never invent these formats.\n32\t- Files allowed to change: `discovery/optimizers/` (new samples + notes)\n33\t- Deliverables: sample files + `discovery/optimizers/format-notes.md`\n34\t- Verification commands: n/a (human)\n35\t- Acceptance criteria: both files verified accepted by the real software; every format question in `integration-contracts.md` answered in writing.\n36\t- Rollback notes: n/a\n37\t- Architect notes: photograph/screenshot software import screens if docs unavailable.\n38\t\n39\t## DIS-002 — Existing Web Quotation Tool Discovery\n40\t\n41\t- Status baseline: pending\n42\t- Recommended model: human + claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (summarization only)\n43\t- Dependencies: none\n44\t- Objective: Document the current quotation tool: capabilities, restrictions (min part size, face orientation), data outputs, integration options.\n45\t- Context: Route D intake; its validation rules must fold into the canonical validation layer, not be duplicated.\n46\t- Scope: screenshots or technical access; list of operational restrictions; export formats it produces.\n47\t- Out of scope: integration implementation.\n48\t- Architectural invariants: none beyond documentation accuracy.\n49\t- Files allowed to change: `discovery/quotation-tool/`\n50\t- Deliverables: `discovery/quotation-tool/notes.md`\n51\t- Verification commands: n/a\n52\t- Acceptance criteria: restriction list complete enough to specify canonical validation rules; integration feasibility stated.\n53\t- Rollback notes: n/a\n54\t- Architect notes: unblocks future Route D ticket; not blocking Phases 1–3.\n55\t\n56\t## DIS-003 — Commercial Inputs Package\n57\t\n58\t- Status baseline: pending\n59\t- Recommended model: human (Management + accountant)\n60\t- Dependencies: none\n61\t- Objective: Collect real commercial inputs: current price tables (panels, cuts by thickness, edge tape/application), customer-supplied-material surcharge rule, current quotation sample, panel-reference catalog, tape types/sizes, transport rules, accountant-validated VAT + withholding treatment, logo + legal company data, delivery terms, avg tickets/day and parts/ticket.\n62\t- Context: master doc §24. Pricing engine (APP-009) configurable but needs real seeds; PDF (APP-010) needs branding/legal.\n63\t- Scope: data collection only.\n64\t- Out of scope: entering data into the system (done via APP-008 UI later).\n65\t- Architectural invariants: never hard-code tax rules; withholding stays configurable until accountant signs off.\n66\t- Files allowed to change: `discovery/commercial/`\n67\t- Deliverables: price spreadsheets, quotation sample, catalog list, tax memo, branding assets.\n68\t- Verification commands: n/a\n69\t- Acceptance criteria: APP-008/009/010 can be seeded without inventing any value.\n70\t- Rollback notes: n/a\n71\t- Architect notes: partial delivery acceptable; missing items become explicit blockers on dependent tickets.\n72\t\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t## Phase 1 — Governance + Operational Control\n76\t\n77\t## GOV-001 — Local Roadmap Execution Dashboard\n78\t\n79\t- Status baseline: pending\n80\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n81\t- Dependencies: none\n82\t- Objective: Localhost-only dashboard that reads this `roadmap.md`, shows Kanban of tickets (To Do / In Progress / Blocked / Completed), safely launches approved executor agents, and writes all runtime evidence outside the roadmap.\n83\t- Context: ADR-003. Full normative spec: `roadmap_dashboard_execution_ticket_en.md` + master doc §27 (both binding).\n84\t- Scope: exactly two source files `tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs` and `tools/roadmap-dashboard/index.html`; runtime artifacts `roadmap-status.md`, `logs/`, `comments/`. Cards show ID, title, short description, dependencies + their completion, recommended model, runtime state. Execute button validates: ticket pending, no active run for ticket, dependencies complete (from ledger, not roadmap text), model/runner allowlisted, ticket still exists in roadmap. Claude runner: `claude --model <id> -p \"<ticket-prompt>\" --output-format stream-json --verbose` with exact IDs `claude-fable-5`, `claude-opus-4-8`, `claude-sonnet-5`. Codex is a separate adapter — if unconfigured, mark blocked with clear message, never pass to `claude --model`. Generated executor prompt enforces the executor rules at the top of this file. Logs to `logs/<ticket>-<timestamp>.log`, viewable from card. Comments `comments/<TICKET>.jsonl`, one JSON object per line (`timestamp, author, type: note|completion|blocked, message`), read before execution. Auto-refresh every few seconds. Listen on `127.0.0.1` only. Startup: `node tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`.\n85\t- Out of scope: authentication, multi-user, remote access, editing roadmap, product code.\n86\t- Architectural invariants: Node 18+; zero external dependencies; spawn with argument arrays, no shell interpolation of client input; explicit model/runner allowlist; ticket-ID validation + path-traversal prevention; one active run per ticket; atomic ledger writes; append-only logs; `roadmap.md` byte-for-byte untouched; history preserved; clear HTTP errors on invalid transitions.\n87\t- Files allowed to change: `tools/roadmap-dashboard/**`, `roadmap-status.md`, `logs/**`, `comments/**`\n88\t- Deliverables: server.mjs, index.html, initialized ledger.\n89\t- Verification commands: `node --check tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`; `node tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs &` then `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:PORT/api/tickets | head`; `shasum roadmap.md` before/after full UI session (must match); attempt execute on ticket with incomplete deps (expect 4xx); attempt Codex run unconfigured (expect blocked state).\n90\t- Acceptance criteria: the 13 criteria in `roadmap_dashboard_execution_ticket_en.md` §Acceptance, all demonstrated in log evidence.\n91\t- Rollback notes: delete `tools/roadmap-dashboard/`; runtime artifacts keep history, do not delete.\n92\t- Architect notes: this ticket gates all other execution; build first.\n93\t\n94\t## INF-001 — Google Sheets Workbook Bootstrap\n95\t\n96\t- Status baseline: pending\n97\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n98\t- Dependencies: [GOV-001]\n99\t- Objective: Create the Panel-Ops workbook with all 16 tabs, exact headers, and seed rows.\n100\t- Context: `data-model.md` is normative. Tabs: Customers, Tickets, Parts, Quotations, Quotation_Lines, Payments, Panel_Prices, Cut_Prices, Edge_Banding_Prices, Users, Workflow_States, Activity, Documents, Configuration, Loss_Reasons, Imports.\n101\t- Scope: Apps Script setup script (idempotent) that creates tabs + headers; seed Workflow_States (17 states per `workflow-state-machine.md`), Configuration keys (`vat_rate=0.19`, `edge_waste_factor=1.10`, `quotation_validity_hours=48`, `aging_alert_minutes=60`, `transition_matrix` JSON generated from `workflow-state-machine.md`, `sequences`, empty `withholding_rules`, empty `company_legal_info`), Loss_Reasons starter list, 3 Users placeholders (roles management/sales/billing).\n102\t- Out of scope: business logic, UI.\n103\t- Architectural invariants: header names exactly per `data-model.md`; no extra columns; script idempotent (safe re-run).\n104\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/setup/**`\n105\t- Deliverables: setup script + run evidence (tab list + header screenshots or logged dump).\n106\t- Verification commands: script self-check function that reads back all tabs/headers and diffs against embedded schema, logging PASS/FAIL per tab.\n107\t- Acceptance criteria: self-check PASS on all 16 tabs; seeds present; re-run makes no changes.\n108\t- Rollback notes: workbook is new; delete workbook to roll back.\n109\t- Architect notes: keep schema constants in one module for reuse by later tickets.\n110\t\n111\t## INF-002 — Apps Script Web App Skeleton (API + Auth + Data Layer)\n112\t\n113\t- Status baseline: pending\n114\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n115\t- Dependencies: [INF-001]\n116\t- Objective: Deployable Web App: session identity from Google account, role resolution from Users tab, JSON API router, generic table read layer, single locked write path, ID sequence generator, Activity writer.\n117\t- Context: every later module builds on this. ADR-002 write-path rule.\n118\t- Scope: `doGet` serves SPA shell; `doPost` JSON API with action routing; `getSession()` (email→role, reject unknown); `db.read(table, filter)`, `db.insert/update(table, row)` wrapped in LockService with atomic sequence increments; `activity.log(...)`; error envelope `{ok:false, error, allowed?}`; deployment config (execute as user accessing, domain-restricted).\n119\t- Out of scope: any business module, UI beyond an authenticated \"hello + role\" shell.\n120\t- Architectural invariants: role checks server-side; unknown user → 403 page; no physical deletes; writes only via locked path.\n121\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/core/**`, `src/gas/api/**`, `src/ui/shell/**`\n122\t- Deliverables: deployed test Web App URL + module code.\n123\t- Verification commands: test function suite (Apps Script) covering: unknown email rejected; sequence increments atomically under loop; insert+read round-trip per table; Activity row appended on write.\n124\t- Acceptance criteria: all tests logged PASS; shell loads showing user email + role.\n125\t- Rollback notes: undeploy web app.\n126\t- Architect notes: this is the foundation — review carefully before accepting.\n127\t\n128\t## INF-003 — Drive Case-File Automation\n129\t\n130\t- Status baseline: pending"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d24f395-8d4d-4147-9711-46f561b0a2bc","uuid":"48ce5349-e1af-4399-b66f-474bd49b0c59","timestamp":"2026-07-18T03:42:56.917Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/work945/Documents/Proyectos/ABM/proyectos/panel-ops/roadmap.md","content":"# Roadmap — Panel-Ops\n**Owner:** Architect AI. This file is the authoritative execution plan.\n**Read-only for executors and the dashboard.** Runtime status lives in `roadmap-status.md`.\nBaseline statuses here are d